dress></addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI HIROO</name> <address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TEIKOKU HORMONE MFG CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, TOMOHITO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KODO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HIROO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TEIKOKU HORMONE MFG. CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJII TOMOHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO KODO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU YASUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI HIROO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJII, TOMOHITO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, KODO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, YASUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAHASHI, HIROO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>In the case of administering an estrogen antagonist for treating or preventing endometriosis and/or menstrual abnormality, it is needless to administer the drug constantly and continuously during the period with a need of the treatment or prevention (i.e., chronic administration) but almost comparable therapeutic effects to those of the chronic administration can be achieved by continuously administering for 5 to 13 days from the menstrual period to immediately before ovulation (i.e., periodic administration). Moreover, the periodic administration is almost completely free from such side effects as observed in the case of the chronic administration of the estrogen antagonist. Thus, the periodic administration is a useful method for administering the estrogen antagonist for treating or preventing endometriosis and/or menstrual abnormality.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Dans le cas d'un antagoniste d'oestrogène destiné au traitement ou à la prévention d'une endométriose et/ou d'un dysfonctionnement menstruel (administration permanente). En effet, on peut obtenir des effets thérapeutiques quasi identiques en administrant le médicament de façon continue pendant 5 à 13 jours du cycle menstruel jusqu'au jour précédant immédiatement l'ovulation (administration périodique). Par ailleurs, l'administration périodique ne s'accompagne de pratiquement aucun des effets secondaires observables dans le cas d'une administration permanente. Ainsi, l'administration périodique constitue un moyen utile d'administrer un antagoniste d'oestrogène pour le traitement ou la prévention d'une endométriose ou d'un dysfonctionnement menstruel.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>